  "proposal": {
    "text": "We use four AI-assisted tools in client work: contract review, legal research and drafting, transcript summaries and translation. No tool we use allows what we enter to be used to train a model. Every tool has a written review step: a person at the firm reviews its output before anyone relies on it. Every tool in use that our known-answer test applies to has a passing result on record. We bill for the time our people spend, not for time a tool saved, and add no separate charge for the tools. Before a tool is used on a matter, we check that client's written terms on AI. Our one-page statement dated 2026-11-25 gives the detail.",
